From 55295d4ea862acc576149c547a906e8801a8a717 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 19:55:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix checkout/migration bugs, add RBAC + rate limiting,
 redesign storefront
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backend fixes:
- Wire the existing order state machine + row locking into the checkout
  API; /orders/{id}/pay was mutating order.state directly with no locking
  and no idempotency guard, so a retried call could double-purchase from
  the provider or double-refund.
- Fix POST /orders returning payment.checkout_url, an attribute that does
  not exist on PaymentIntent (the field is payment_url) - every order
  creation crashed with AttributeError against the real (non-demo) API.
  No test exercised the actual HTTP endpoint, so this had never been
  caught.
- Fix alembic: CREATE TYPE orderstate was emitted twice on a fresh
  database (once from an explicit .create(checkfirst=True) call, again
  implicitly while compiling CREATE TABLE orders), failing every clean
  `alembic upgrade head`. Separately, env.py's async migration runner
  split context.configure()/run_migrations() across two connection.run_sync
  calls with no context.begin_transaction() wrapper, so on success the
  whole migration silently rolled back (exit 0, empty database). Fixed
  both against a real Postgres instance.
- Fix CORS: allow_origins=["*"] + allow_credentials=True is a combination
  browsers refuse to honor; now an explicit allow-list with credentials
  off (nothing here uses cookies).
- Encrypt DigitalDelivery.encrypted_payload at rest (Fernet, keyed by
  DELIVERY_ENCRYPTION_KEY) instead of storing the gift-card secret in
  plaintext, and audit every reveal - both required by docs/SECURITY.md
  but unimplemented.
- Add an API-key-gated admin router (orders, audit log, variant
  enable/disable) and a public /api/v1/categories endpoint + category
  filter on /api/v1/products - the PRD's Admin scope and category
  discovery existed only on paper.
- Add Redis-backed rate limiting on quotes/orders/pay/order-read
  (fail-open if Redis is unreachable, so it can't take down checkout).
- New apps/api/tests/test_api_integration.py drives the real HTTP
  endpoints end-to-end (idempotent pay, encryption at rest, admin auth,
  category filtering) instead of only the service layer underneath them.

Frontend fixes + redesign:
- app/page.tsx was still the pre-Tailwind prototype: classnames like
  .hero/.card/.button/.checkout don't exist anywhere, so the storefront
  rendered unstyled. Meanwhile a complete, accessible component system
  (Hero, SiteHeader, ProductGrid/ProductCard, CheckoutSheet, Countdown,
  OrderTimeline, DeliveryReveal) plus lib/api.ts's demo-mode fallback sat
  entirely unused. Rewired page.tsx to compose the real components.
- Redesigned the token layer toward an Apple.com-like language: near-white
  canvas, near-black text, one confident blue for anything actionable,
  pill-shaped primary CTAs, hairline borders + soft elevation instead of
  heavy borders, centered hero. Verified by screenshot in demo mode
  through the full purchase flow.
- Added category tabs (گیفت‌کارت/اشتراک/بازی/نرم‌افزار) above the existing
  brand filter in ProductGrid - the PRD explicitly lists category
  discovery as required customer scope; only brand filtering existed.
- Upgraded Next 14.2.32 -> 15.5.23 and React 18 -> 19: npm audit showed
  several disclosed high-severity DoS advisories on the old range whose
  fixes only land in the 15.5.x line. This app has no dynamic routes,
  server actions, or cookies/headers usage, so migration risk was low;
  verified via tsc, a clean install, and a rendered smoke test. Added an
  npm override to also patch Next's bundled internal postcss.
- Added a Content-Security-Policy header (present in intent per
  docs/SECURITY.md, absent in next.config.mjs).

